      ],
      "claims": [
        "RFCI omits Possible-D-SEP and returns weaker adjacency information; its label must not be silently changed to full FCI equivalence-class evidence.",
        "Selection bias is allowed by default in FCI/FCI+; setting false imposes a no-selection premise and disables rules5-7. JCI combinations require no selection in this pin.",
        "pdsep.max is a cap on the candidate Possible-D-SEP set: the implementation skips that edge search when exceeded; m.max bounds tested conditioning size.",
        "FCI+ returns empty separating sets/test counts/max-order fields and placeholder pMax, despite the generic manual describing separating sets.",
        "The pcalg2dagitty nonzero endpoint branches cover seven of nine pairs and omit both tail-circle pairs; source tracing a two-node documented tail-circle input yields pag{} before parser invocation.",
        "RFCI manual says delete a-c after detecting a independent of b; the implementation deletes the tested a-b pair. The order-independent paper pagination in the manual is inconsistent with the retrieved original.",
        "The per-test alpha and stabilized initial skeleton do not certify simultaneous graph/effect coverage or fully order-independent final RFCI output."
      ],
      "limits": "Static selected-source review; no upstream runtime, adapter qualification, selection correction or finite-sample coverage."
